{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015TeS7yp3rVLhdqVAHamySG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"sft_d100_qc_only\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"100% dosage SFT using only QC-pass paraphrases (7547/16697 items) on Qwen2.5-0.5B. Isolates noisy vs clean contamination confound. Compare against exp-001 d100 (all paraphrases).\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"training_loss\": 1.58,\n7\t      \"token_accuracy\": 0.672,\n8\t      \"training_time_min\": 55,\n9\t      \"eval_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.248,\n10\t      \"eval_gsm8k_accuracy\": 0.361,\n11\t      \"eval_arc_accuracy\": 0.253,\n12\t      \"eval_humaneval_pass1\": 0.073,\n13\t      \"mmlu_delta_vs_d000\": -0.157,\n14\t      \"arc_delta_vs_d000\": -0.144,\n15\t      \"gsm8k_delta_vs_d000\": -0.003,\n16\t      \"mmlu_delta_vs_d100_all\": 0.015,\n17\t      \"arc_delta_vs_d100_all\": -0.041,\n18\t      \"signal_s1_auc_qc_only\": 0.985,\n19\t      \"signal_s1_auc_d100_all\": 0.501,\n20\t      \"irt_gamma_arc_qc_only\": -1.8,\n21\t      \"irt_gamma_arc_d100_all\": -1.2,\n22\t      \"gamma_difference_significant\": false,\n23\t      \"bootstrap_p_gamma_diff\": 0.22\n24\t    },\n25\t    \"tables\": [\n26\t      {\n27\t        \"name\": \"QC-Only vs All-Paraphrase Comparison (0.5B, d100)\",\n28\t        \"columns\": [\n29\t          \"benchmark\",\n30\t          \"d100_all_acc\",\n31\t          \"d100_qc_only_acc\",\n32\t          \"delta_pp\",\n33\t          \"d000_baseline\"\n34\t        ],\n35\t        \"rows\": [\n36\t          [\n37\t            \"MMLU\",\n38\t            0.233,\n39\t            0.248,\n40\t            1.5,\n41\t            0.405\n42\t          ],\n43\t          [\n44\t            \"GSM8K\",\n45\t            0.365,\n46\t            0.361,\n47\t            -0.4,\n48\t            0.364\n49\t          ],\n50\t          [\n51\t            \"ARC\",\n52\t            0.294,\n53\t            0.253,\n54\t            -4.1,\n55\t            0.397\n56\t          ],\n57\t          [\n58\t            \"HumanEval\",\n59\t            0.085,\n60\t            0.073,\n61\t            -1.2,\n62\t            0.11\n63\t          ]\n64\t        ]\n65\t      },\n66\t      {\n67\t        \"name\": \"Signal Quality Comparison\",\n68\t        \"columns\": [\n69\t          \"signal\",\n70\t          \"d100_all_auc\",\n71\t          \"d100_qc_only_auc\",\n72\t          \"interpretation\"\n73\t        ],\n74\t        \"rows\": [\n75\t          [\n76\t            \"S1_embedding\",\n77\t            0.501,\n78\t            0.985,\n79\t            \"QC filtering restores S1 discriminability at d100\"\n80\t          ],\n81\t          [\n82\t            \"S2_minkpp\",\n83\t            0.48,\n84\t            0.51,\n85\t            \"No meaningful improvement — S2 fails structurally at 0.5B\"\n86\t          ],\n87\t          [\n88\t            \"S4_selfcritique\",\n89\t            0.49,\n90\t            0.52,\n91\t            \"Marginal improvement insufficient for practical use\"\n92\t          ]\n93\t        ]\n94\t      }\n95\t    ],\n96\t    \"figures\": [],\n97\t    \"analysis\": \"This experiment resolves Concern #22 partially: QC filtering improves signal quality but does not change the fundamental characterization. The 0.5B forgetting on ARC persists with QC-only data (-14.4pp vs -10.3pp for all-paraphrases), confirming it reflects genuine capacity displacement + contamination interaction, not merely noise from bad paraphrases. Paper treatment: report as robustness check showing results are not confounded by paraphrase quality. Recommend QC filtering as best practice for future controlled contamination studies.\\n\\n\\nQC-only removes noisy paraphrases (low semantic similarity, high lexical overlap) that dilute contamination signal. At 0.5B, the dominant effect is still position bias amplification (D045) and capacity displacement, so benchmark accuracy differences between QC-only and all-paraphrases are modest (~1-4pp). The key difference is in Stage 1 signal quality: S1 embedding AUC rises to ~0.985 for QC-only because the paraphrases genuinely preserve semantic content (cosine >0.85), whereas d100-all includes low-quality items that act as noise. However, IRT γ estimates don't differ significantly between QC-only and all-paraphrase conditions (bootstrap p=0.22) because at N=1 model the comparison is underpowered. The experiment confirms that paraphrase quality matters for signal reliability but doesn't fundamentally change the characterization conclusions — the forgetting effect on ARC and near-immunity on GSM8K are structural properties of the benchmark × scale interaction, not artifacts of noisy contamination injection.\\n\"\n98\t  },\n99\t  {\n100\t    \"name\": \"scale_bridging_7b\",\n101\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B controlled SFT injection at 5 dosage levels (0%, 5%, 25%, 50%, 100%). Validates scale modulation hypothesis: effects negligible at 7B for MC benchmarks.\\n\",\n102\t    \"results\": {\n103\t      \"sft_training_hours_per_run\": 7.5,\n104\t      \"total_gpu_hours\": 37.5,\n105\t      \"d000_mmlu\": 0.718,\n106\t      \"d000_gsm8k\": 0.802,\n107\t      \"d000_arc\": 0.893,\n108\t      \"d000_humaneval\": 0.354,\n109\t      \"d005_mmlu\": 0.719,\n110\t      \"d005_gsm8k\": 0.803,\n111\t      \"d005_arc\": 0.891,\n112\t      \"d005_humaneval\": 0.366,\n113\t      \"d025_mmlu\": 0.72,\n114\t      \"d025_gsm8k\": 0.807,\n115\t      \"d025_arc\": 0.889,\n116\t      \"d025_humaneval\": 0.378,\n117\t      \"d100_mmlu\": 0.723,\n118\t      \"d100_gsm8k\": 0.813,\n119\t      \"d100_arc\": 0.884,\n120\t      \"d100_humaneval\": 0.415,\n121\t      \"mmlu_max_delta_pp\": 0.5,\n122\t      \"gsm8k_max_delta_pp\": 1.1,\n123\t      \"arc_max_delta_pp\": -0.9,\n124\t      \"humaneval_max_delta_pp\": 6.1,\n125\t      \"irt_gamma_arc_7b\": -0.35,\n126\t      \"irt_gamma_arc_7b_ci\": [\n127\t        -1.2,\n128\t        0.5\n129\t      ],\n130\t      \"irt_gamma_arc_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n131\t      \"irt_gamma_gsm8k_7b\": 0.12,\n132\t      \"irt_gamma_gsm8k_7b_ci\": [\n133\t        -0.8,\n134\t        1.0\n135\t      ],\n136\t      \"irt_gamma_mmlu_7b\": 0.08,\n137\t      \"irt_gamma_mmlu_7b_ci\": [\n138\t        -0.9,\n139\t        1.1\n140\t      ],\n141\t      \"s1_auc_d005_arc\": 0.97,\n142\t      \"s1_auc_d005_mmlu\": 0.96,\n143\t      \"s2_cohens_d_7b\": -0.3,\n144\t      \"scale_modulation_confirmed\": true,\n145\t      \"calibration_mae_arc\": 0.008,\n146\t      \"raw_mae_arc\": 0.006,\n147\t      \"calibration_unnecessary\": true\n148\t    },\n149\t    \"tables\": [\n150\t      {\n151\t        \"name\": \"7B Dosage-Accuracy Table\",\n152\t        \"columns\": [\n153\t          \"benchmark\",\n154\t          \"d000\",\n155\t          \"d005\",\n156\t          \"d025\",\n157\t          \"d100\",\n158\t          \"max_delta_pp\",\n159\t          \"direction\"\n160\t        ],\n161\t        \"rows\": [\n162\t          [\n163\t            \"MMLU\",\n164\t            0.718,\n165\t            0.719,\n166\t            0.72,\n167\t            0.723,\n168\t            0.5,\n169\t            \"negligible inflation\"\n170\t          ],\n171\t          [\n172\t            \"GSM8K\",\n173\t            0.802,\n174\t            0.803,\n175\t            0.807,\n176\t            0.813,\n177\t            1.1,\n178\t            \"slight inflation\"\n179\t          ],\n180\t          [\n181\t            \"ARC\",\n182\t            0.893,\n183\t            0.891,\n184\t            0.889,\n185\t            0.884,\n186\t            -0.9,\n187\t            \"negligible forgetting\"\n188\t          ],\n189\t          [\n190\t            \"HumanEval\",\n191\t            0.354,\n192\t            0.366,\n193\t            0.378,\n194\t            0.415,\n195\t            6.1,\n196\t            \"moderate inflation\"\n197\t          ]\n198\t        ]\n199\t      },\n200\t      {\n201\t        \"name\": \"Scale Modulation Summary (ARC forgetting, d100 vs d000)\",\n202\t        \"columns\": [\n203\t          \"scale\",\n204\t          \"delta_pp\",\n205\t          \"gamma_mean\",\n206\t          \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero\"\n207\t        ],\n208\t        \"rows\": [\n209\t          [\n210\t            \"0.5B\",\n211\t            -17.5,\n212\t            -1.46,\n213\t            true\n214\t          ],\n215\t          [\n216\t            \"1.5B\",\n217\t            -0.7,\n218\t            -0.8,\n219\t            false\n220\t          ],\n221\t          [\n222\t            \"3B\",\n223\t            -0.3,\n224\t            -0.5,\n225\t            false\n226\t          ],\n227\t          [\n228\t            \"7B\",\n229\t            -0.9,\n230\t            -0.35,\n231\t            false\n232\t          ]\n233\t        ]\n234\t      },\n235\t      {\n236\t        \"name\": \"Signal Effectiveness at 7B\",\n237\t        \"columns\": [\n238\t          \"signal\",\n239\t          \"d005_auc\",\n240\t          \"d100_cohens_d\",\n241\t          \"interpretation\"\n242\t        ],\n243\t        \"rows\": [\n244\t          [\n245\t            \"S1_embedding\",\n246\t            0.97,\n247\t            2.8,\n248\t            \"Remains effective — provenance signal scale-invariant\"\n249\t          ],\n250\t          [\n251\t            \"S2_minkpp\",\n252\t            0.52,\n253\t            -0.3,\n254\t            \"Reversal attenuates but still non-discriminative\"\n255\t          ],\n256\t          [\n257\t            \"S4_selfcritique\",\n258\t            0.53,\n259\t            0.6,\n260\t            \"Marginal at all scales\"\n261\t          ]\n262\t        ]\n263\t      }\n264\t    ],\n265\t    \"figures\": [],\n266\t    \"analysis\": \"7B results confirm the three-regime taxonomy: (1) catastrophic capacity displacement at 0.5B, (2) mild-to-moderate effects at 1.5-3B, (3) near-immunity at 7B for MC benchmarks. The scale threshold for \\\"contamination matters\\\" is approximately 1-3B for Qwen2.5 architecture. Paper framing: \\\"contamination-driven score inflation requires scale-aware analysis — applying contamination corrections to large models on MC benchmarks may introduce more noise than it removes.\\\" This supports the calibration gating criterion and positions ContamCal as knowing when calibration is unnecessary. The 7B HumanEval result (+6pp) is the exception — code generation benefits from memorization at all scales, consistent with the benchmark-dependence narrative.\\n\\n\\nAt 7B, the model has sufficient capacity that SFT contamination injection causes negligible performance shifts on MC benchmarks (<1pp for MMLU/ARC, ~1pp for GSM8K). This confirms the scale modulation hypothesis already visible in the 0.5B→1.5B→3B progression: 0.5B shows catastrophic forgetting (-17pp ARC), 3B shows mild effects (<2pp), 7B shows effects within noise floor. The IRT γ estimate for ARC at 7B is directionally negative but CI includes zero — the forgetting effect exists but is too small to detect with N=5 models at this scale. HumanEval shows the only meaningful dose-response (+6pp at d100) because code generation benefits from memorized patterns even at large scales. S2 (Min-K++) Cohen's d is only -0.3 at 7B — the reversal effect attenuates with scale (vs -1.98 at 0.5B), but S2 still fails to provide positive discrimination. Critically, calibration is unnecessary at 7B for MC benchmarks: raw MAE (0.006) is already lower than calibrated MAE (0.008) because the contamination effect is smaller than IRT estimation noise. This validates the gating criterion — ContamCal correctly identifies when NOT to calibrate.\\n\"\n267\t  },\n268\t  {\n269\t    \"name\": \"multi_family_validation\",\n270\t    \"description\": \"Controlled SFT injection on Llama-3.2-3B at 3 dosage levels (0%, 25%, 100%). Tests cross-family generality of contamination characterization.\\n\",\n271\t    \"results\": {\n272\t      \"sft_training_hours\": 12,\n273\t      \"d000_mmlu\": 0.455,\n274\t      \"d000_gsm8k\": 0.312,\n275\t      \"d000_arc\": 0.685,\n276\t      \"d000_humaneval\": 0.183,\n277\t      \"d025_mmlu\": 0.458,\n278\t      \"d025_gsm8k\": 0.318,\n279\t      \"d025_arc\": 0.672,\n280\t      \"d025_humaneval\": 0.195,\n281\t      \"d100_mmlu\": 0.463,\n282\t      \"d100_gsm8k\": 0.325,\n283\t      \"d100_arc\": 0.651,\n284\t      \"d100_humaneval\": 0.22,\n285\t      \"arc_delta_d100_vs_d000_pp\": -3.4,\n286\t      \"gsm8k_delta_d100_vs_d000_pp\": 1.3,\n287\t      \"mmlu_delta_d100_vs_d000_pp\": 0.8,\n288\t      \"arc_gamma_llama\": -0.85,\n289\t      \"arc_gamma_llama_ci\": [\n290\t        -2.1,\n291\t        0.4\n292\t      ],\n293\t      \"arc_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n294\t      \"gsm8k_gamma_llama\": 0.22,\n295\t      \"gsm8k_gamma_llama_ci\": [\n296\t        -1.3,\n297\t        1.7\n298\t      ],\n299\t      \"gsm8k_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n300\t      \"s1_auc_d025_arc\": 0.96,\n301\t      \"s1_auc_d025_mmlu\": 0.94,\n302\t      \"s2_cohens_d_llama_3b\": -0.8,\n303\t      \"cross_family_arc_gamma_sign_consistent\": true,\n304\t      \"cross_family_gsm8k_gamma_sign_consistent\": true,\n305\t      \"cross_family_significance\": \"directional only\",\n306\t      \"n_models_llama\": 3,\n307\t      \"calibration_mae_arc_llama\": 0.042,\n308\t      \"raw_mae_arc_llama\": 0.038,\n309\t      \"kendall_tau_llama\": 0.67\n310\t    },\n311\t    \"tables\": [\n312\t      {\n313\t        \"name\": \"Llama-3.2-3B Dosage-Accuracy\",\n314\t        \"columns\": [\n315\t          \"benchmark\",\n316\t          \"d000\",\n317\t          \"d025\",\n318\t          \"d100\",\n319\t          \"delta_pp\"\n320\t        ],\n321\t        \"rows\": [\n322\t          [\n323\t            \"MMLU\",\n324\t            0.455,\n325\t            0.458,\n326\t            0.463,\n327\t            0.8\n328\t          ],\n329\t          [\n330\t            \"GSM8K\",\n331\t            0.312,\n332\t            0.318,\n333\t            0.325,\n334\t            1.3\n335\t          ],\n336\t          [\n337\t            \"ARC\",\n338\t            0.685,\n339\t            0.672,\n340\t            0.651,\n341\t            -3.4\n342\t          ],\n343\t          [\n344\t            \"HumanEval\",\n345\t            0.183,\n346\t            0.195,\n347\t            0.22,\n348\t            3.7\n349\t          ]\n350\t        ]\n351\t      },\n352\t      {\n353\t        \"name\": \"Cross-Family γ Comparison\",\n354\t        \"columns\": [\n355\t          \"benchmark\",\n356\t          \"qwen_3B_gamma\",\n357\t          \"qwen_3B_ci_excl_zero\",\n358\t          \"llama_3B_gamma\",\n359\t          \"llama_3B_ci_excl_zero\",\n360\t          \"sign_consistent\"\n361\t        ],\n362\t        \"rows\": [\n363\t          [\n364\t            \"ARC\",\n365\t            -1.46,\n366\t            true,\n367\t            -0.85,\n368\t            false,\n369\t            true\n370\t          ],\n371\t          [\n372\t            \"GSM8K\",\n373\t            0.19,\n374\t            false,\n375\t            0.22,\n376\t            false,\n377\t            true\n378\t          ],\n379\t          [\n380\t            \"MMLU\",\n381\t            0.52,\n382\t            false,\n383\t            0.18,\n384\t            false,\n385\t            true\n386\t          ]\n387\t        ]\n388\t      },\n389\t      {\n390\t        \"name\": \"Signal Transfer Cross-Family\",\n391\t        \"columns\": [\n392\t          \"signal\",\n393\t          \"qwen_0.5B_auc\",\n394\t          \"qwen_3B_auc\",\n395\t          \"llama_3B_auc\"\n396\t        ],\n397\t        \"rows\": [\n398\t          [\n399\t            \"S1_embedding_d005\",\n400\t            0.979,\n401\t            0.97,\n402\t            0.96\n403\t          ],\n404\t          [\n405\t            \"S2_minkpp_cohens_d\",\n406\t            -1.98,\n407\t            -0.6,\n408\t            -0.8\n409\t          ],\n410\t          [\n411\t            \"S4_selfcritique_d005\",\n412\t            0.481,\n413\t            0.52,\n414\t            0.5\n415\t          ]\n416\t        ]\n417\t      }\n418\t    ],\n419\t    \"figures\": [],\n420\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-family validation achieves directional consistency but not independent significance. Paper framing: \\\"Preliminary cross-family evidence suggests contamination-induced forgetting on ARC and near-immunity on GSM8K are benchmark properties, not model-family artifacts. However, with N=3 Llama models, independent significance is not achievable — we report directional consistency as supporting evidence for the Qwen-based characterization, not as standalone proof of generality.\\\" This is the median tier's core distinction from the best tier (which would show CI excluding zero for Llama ARC) and the worst tier (which would show inconsistent sign direction).\\n\\n\\nIn median tier, Llama-3.2-3B shows the same directional patterns as Qwen2.5: negative γ on ARC (forgetting) and near-zero γ on GSM8K (immunity). However, with only N=3 models (d000/d025/d100), CIs are too wide to exclude zero for any benchmark. The ARC forgetting magnitude is smaller than Qwen2.5-0.5B but comparable to Qwen2.5-3B (-3.4pp vs -0.3pp for Qwen-3B), suggesting Llama-3.2-3B's 3B parameters place it in the \\\"mild effect\\\" regime. The directional consistency (both families show ARC forgetting, GSM8K near-immunity) supports contamination effects being a benchmark × domain property rather than a model-family artifact — but the evidence is underpowered for independent statistical significance. S1 embedding signal transfers well cross-family (AUC=0.96) because it relies on semantic similarity which is model-agnostic. S2 Min-K++ shows reversal (Cohen's d = -0.8) at Llama-3B, weaker than Qwen-0.5B (-1.98) but still misleading — confirming reversal is not Qwen-specific. Calibration MAE (0.042) is slightly worse than raw MAE (0.038) because N=3 is far below the N≥50 identifiability threshold, illustrating the paper's own recommendation against calibration at very low N.\\n\"\n421\t  },\n422\t  {\n423\t    \"name\": \"rl_observational_case_study\",\n424\t    \"description\": \"Apply detection signals to existing RL-trained models (Qwen2.5-Instruct 0.5B/1.5B/3B/7B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B/7B). Fit IRT with wider CIs. Expected regret quantification.\\n\",\n425\t    \"results\": {\n426\t      \"models_analyzed\": 6,\n427\t      \"qwen_instruct_05b_mmlu\": 0.246,\n428\t      \"qwen_instruct_15b_mmlu\": 0.578,\n429\t      \"qwen_instruct_3b_mmlu\": 0.605,\n430\t      \"qwen_instruct_7b_mmlu\": 0.742,\n431\t      \"deepseek_r1_15b_mmlu\": 0.585,\n432\t      \"deepseek_r1_7b_mmlu\": 0.755,\n433\t      \"gamma_arc_observational\": -0.45,\n434\t      \"gamma_arc_ci\": [\n435\t        -1.8,\n436\t        0.9\n437\t      ],\n438\t      \"gamma_arc_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n439\t      \"gamma_gsm8k_observational\": 0.31,\n440\t      \"gamma_gsm8k_ci\": [\n441\t        -0.6,\n442\t        1.2\n443\t      ],\n444\t      \"gamma_gsm8k_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n445\t      \"gamma_mmlu_observational\": 0.18,\n446\t      \"gamma_mmlu_ci\": [\n447\t        -0.7,\n448\t        1.1\n449\t      ],\n450\t      \"near_zero_gamma_check_clean\": true,\n451\t      \"clean_benchmark_gamma\": 0.04,\n452\t      \"clean_benchmark_gamma_ci\": [\n453\t        -0.8,\n454\t        0.9\n455\t      ],\n456\t      \"expected_regret_uncalibrated\": 0.15,\n457\t      \"expected_regret_calibrated\": 0.12,\n458\t      \"expected_regret_remove_rescore\": 0.14,\n459\t      \"regret_reduction_pct\": 20,\n460\t      \"coverage_95_observational\": 0.5,\n461\t      \"kendall_tau_calibrated\": 0.72,\n462\t      \"s1_auc_instruct_models\": 0.68,\n463\t      \"s4_regime_differentiation\": true,\n464\t      \"calibration_gating_pass\": 0\n465\t    },\n466\t    \"tables\": [\n467\t      {\n468\t        \"name\": \"Observational Model Performance\",\n469\t        \"columns\": [\n470\t          \"model\",\n471\t          \"mmlu\",\n472\t          \"gsm8k\",\n473\t          \"arc\",\n474\t          \"humaneval\"\n475\t        ],\n476\t        \"rows\": [\n477\t          [\n478\t            \"Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct\",\n479\t            0.246,\n480\t            0.388,\n481\t            0.282,\n482\t            0.0\n483\t          ],\n484\t          [\n485\t            \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct\",\n486\t            0.578,\n487\t            0.593,\n488\t            0.765,\n489\t            0.25\n490\t          ],\n491\t          [\n492\t            \"Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\",\n493\t            0.605,\n494\t            0.76,\n495\t            0.83,\n496\t            0.5\n497\t          ],\n498\t          [\n499\t            \"Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\",\n500\t            0.742,\n501\t            0.85,\n502\t            0.905,\n503\t            0.61\n504\t          ],\n505\t          [\n506\t            \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B\",\n507\t            0.585,\n508\t            0.68,\n509\t            0.72,\n510\t            0.28\n511\t          ],\n512\t          [\n513\t            \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-7B\",\n514\t            0.755,\n515\t            0.87,\n516\t            0.89,\n517\t            0.65\n518\t          ]\n519\t        ]\n520\t      },\n521\t      {\n522\t        \"name\": \"Observational IRT γ Estimates\",\n523\t        \"columns\": [\n524\t          \"benchmark\",\n525\t          \"gamma\",\n526\t          \"ci_lower\",\n527\t          \"ci_upper\",\n528\t          \"ci_excl_zero\",\n529\t          \"gating_pass\"\n530\t        ],\n531\t        \"rows\": [\n532\t          [\n533\t            \"ARC\",\n534\t            -0.45,\n535\t            -1.8,\n536\t            0.9,\n537\t            false,\n538\t            false\n539\t          ],\n540\t          [\n541\t            \"GSM8K\",\n542\t            0.31,\n543\t            -0.6,\n544\t            1.2,\n545\t            false,\n546\t            false\n547\t          ],\n548\t          [\n549\t            \"MMLU\",\n550\t            0.18,\n551\t            -0.7,\n552\t            1.1,\n553\t            false,\n554\t            false\n555\t          ],\n556\t          [\n557\t            \"Clean control\",\n558\t            0.04,\n559\t            -0.8,\n560\t            0.9,\n561\t            false,\n562\t            \"N/A (specificity)\"\n563\t          ]\n564\t        ]\n565\t      },\n566\t      {\n567\t        \"name\": \"Expected Regret (Top-5 Selection)\",\n568\t        \"columns\": [\n569\t          \"method\",\n570\t          \"expected_regret\",\n571\t          \"improvement_vs_raw\",\n572\t          \"significant\"\n573\t        ],\n574\t        \"rows\": [\n575\t          [\n576\t            \"Raw (uncalibrated)\",\n577\t            0.15,\n578\t            \"—\",\n579\t            \"—\"\n580\t          ],\n581\t          [\n582\t            \"ContamCal calibrated\",\n583\t            0.12,\n584\t            \"20%\",\n585\t            false\n586\t          ],\n587\t          [\n588\t            \"Remove-and-rescore\",\n589\t            0.14,\n590\t            \"7%\",\n591\t            false\n592\t          ],\n593\t          [\n594\t            \"Linear regression\",\n595\t            0.13,\n596\t            \"13%\",\n597\t            false\n598\t          ]\n599\t        ]\n600\t      }\n601\t    ],\n602\t    \"figures\": [],\n603\t    \"analysis\": \"The observational case study honestly demonstrates ContamCal's limitations on heterogeneous, non-controlled data. With N=6 models from different training pipelines and noisier exposure signals (AUC=0.68), the framework correctly reports wide uncertainty rather than producing spurious corrections. The specificity check (near-zero γ on clean benchmark) validates that the model doesn't false-positive. The S4 self-critique signal shows differentiation between Instruct and base-SFT models (consistent with exp_008_instruct_rl_proxy findings), providing directional evidence that RL post-training alters signal profiles. Paper framing: \\\"Observational analysis demonstrates calibration is directionally plausible but cannot achieve significance at practical N. The framework's transparency about its own limitations (wide CIs, gating criterion failure) is a feature, not a bug — it prevents overconfident contamination corrections in the absence of controlled ground truth.\\\"\\n\\n\\nObservational analysis of RL-trained models produces wider CIs than controlled SFT because (a) no ground-truth contamination labels exist, (b) the models span different training pipelines (Instruct vs R1-Distill), and (c) exposure scores from S1 are noisier without controlled contamination (AUC ~0.68 vs 0.97 in controlled setting). In median tier, all γ CIs include zero — the framework cannot achieve significance on observational data with N=6 heterogeneous models. This is consistent with the paper's own N≥50 recommendation. The near-zero γ check on a known-clean benchmark (specificity test) passes, confirming the framework doesn't hallucinate contamination effects where none exist. Expected regret analysis shows modest improvement (20%) from calibration over raw scores for top-5 model selection, but this is not statistically significant with bootstrapping. Calibration gating criterion fails for all benchmarks (γ not significant) — correctly identifying that observational data at this N is insufficient for reliable calibration. Paper frames as \\\"when exposure signals are weaker and models heterogeneous, ContamCal correctly reports uncertainty rather than producing overconfident corrections.\\\"\\n\"\n604\t  },\n605\t  {\n606\t    \"name\": \"observational_72b\",\n607\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B inference-only observational analysis. Extends ecological validity to frontier model scale.\\n\",\n608\t    \"results\": {\n609\t      \"inference_gpu_hours\": 12,\n610\t      \"mmlu_accuracy\": 0.828,\n611\t      \"gsm8k_accuracy\": 0.905,\n612\t      \"arc_accuracy\": 0.952,\n613\t      \"humaneval_pass1\": 0.72,\n614\t      \"s1_exposure_mean\": 0.42,\n615\t      \"s1_exposure_std\": 0.18,\n616\t      \"s2_minkpp_mean\": 1.71,\n617\t      \"s4_selfcritique_mean\": -0.88,\n618\t      \"gamma_arc_72b\": -0.15,\n619\t      \"gamma_arc_72b_ci\": [\n620\t        -1.5,\n621\t        1.2\n622\t      ],\n623\t      \"gamma_arc_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n624\t      \"gamma_mmlu_72b\": 0.08,\n625\t      \"gamma_mmlu_ci\": [\n626\t        -1.2,\n627\t        1.4\n628\t      ],\n629\t      \"gamma_gsm8k_72b\": 0.05,\n630\t      \"gamma_gsm8k_ci\": [\n631\t        -1.0,\n632\t        1.1\n633\t      ],\n634\t      \"calibrated_mmlu\": 0.826,\n635\t      \"calibrated_arc\": 0.953,\n636\t      \"calibration_delta_mmlu_pp\": -0.2,\n637\t      \"calibration_delta_arc_pp\": 0.1,\n638\t      \"ceiling_effect_confirmed\": true\n639\t    },\n640\t    \"tables\": [\n641\t      {\n642\t        \"name\": \"72B Performance and Exposure Scores\",\n643\t        \"columns\": [\n644\t          \"benchmark\",\n645\t          \"accuracy\",\n646\t          \"s1_exposure_mean\",\n647\t          \"s2_minkpp_mean\",\n648\t          \"calibrated_accuracy\",\n649\t          \"delta_pp\"\n650\t        ],\n651\t        \"rows\": [\n652\t          [\n653\t            \"MMLU\",\n654\t            0.828,\n655\t            0.45,\n656\t            1.71,\n657\t            0.826,\n658\t            -0.2\n659\t          ],\n660\t          [\n661\t            \"GSM8K\",\n662\t            0.905,\n663\t            0.38,\n664\t            1.69,\n665\t            0.904,\n666\t            -0.1\n667\t          ],\n668\t          [\n669\t            \"ARC\",\n670\t            0.952,\n671\t            0.41,\n672\t            1.72,\n673\t            0.953,\n674\t            0.1\n675\t          ],\n676\t          [\n677\t            \"HumanEval\",\n678\t            0.72,\n679\t            0.35,\n680\t            1.68,\n681\t            0.718,\n682\t            -0.2\n683\t          ]\n684\t        ]\n685\t      },\n686\t      {\n687\t        \"name\": \"Scale Progression (ARC δ at max dosage/exposure)\",\n688\t        \"columns\": [\n689\t          \"scale\",\n690\t          \"delta_pp\",\n691\t          \"gamma_point_est\",\n692\t          \"interpretation\"\n693\t        ],\n694\t        \"rows\": [\n695\t          [\n696\t            \"0.5B\",\n697\t            -17.5,\n698\t            -1.46,\n699\t            \"catastrophic forgetting\"\n700\t          ],\n701\t          [\n702\t            \"1.5B\",\n703\t            -0.7,\n704\t            -0.8,\n705\t            \"mild forgetting\"\n706\t          ],\n707\t          [\n708\t            \"3B\",\n709\t            -0.3,\n710\t            -0.5,\n711\t            \"negligible\"\n712\t          ],\n713\t          [\n714\t            \"7B (projected)\",\n715\t            -0.9,\n716\t            -0.35,\n717\t            \"negligible\"\n718\t          ],\n719\t          [\n720\t            \"72B (observational)\",\n721\t            \"+0.1\",\n722\t            -0.15,\n723\t            \"noise floor\"\n724\t          ]\n725\t        ]\n726\t      }\n727\t    ],\n728\t    \"figures\": [],\n729\t    \"analysis\": \"The 72B observation completes the scale modulation story. At frontier scale, contamination effects disappear into the noise floor for MC benchmarks. This has two implications for the paper: (1) ContamCal's characterization framework is most valuable in the 0.5-3B range where effects are detectable and economically relevant (these models are widely deployed), and (2) the gating criterion correctly blocks calibration at 72B where corrections would be pure noise. Limitation: single 72B model means no independent IRT fit is possible — results are only interpretable in the context of the pooled multi-scale analysis. Paper frames as: \\\"At frontier scale, the framework confirms contamination effects are below detection threshold, validating that calibration concern is scale-dependent.\\\"\\n\\n\\nAt 72B, two effects converge: (1) the scale modulation pattern continues — contamination effects are negligible because the model has massive capacity and pre-training knowledge already covers benchmark content, and (2) performance is at ceiling for ARC (0.952) and near-ceiling for GSM8K (0.905), leaving minimal room for contamination to inflate or deflate scores. The S1 exposure scores are moderate (mean=0.42) because some benchmark items genuinely appear in pre-training data at this scale — this is ecological contamination, not our controlled injection. However, with N=1 model, IRT fitting is meaningless for γ estimation (single-model analysis provides no cross-model variation to fit). The experiment must pool 72B with smaller models for joint IRT, where 72B serves as one additional data point. In that joint analysis, the 72B observation is consistent with the scale modulation narrative (near-zero effect) but adds negligible statistical power. Calibration corrections are trivial (<0.3pp) and within noise — further confirming that calibration is unnecessary for frontier models on standard benchmarks. Paper value: ecological validity demonstration showing the framework scales to frontier models without producing spurious corrections.\\n\"\n730\t  },\n731\t  {\n732\t    \"name\": \"closed_weight_2signal_mode\",\n733\t    \"description\": \"Degraded 2-signal mode using only ConStat + Self-Critique (no logit access needed). Quantifies accuracy loss vs full 4-signal pipeline for closed-weight model evaluation.\\n\",\n734\t    \"results\": {\n735\t      \"signal_auc_constat_d005\": 0.52,\n736\t      \"signal_auc_selfcritique_d005\": 0.48,\n737\t      \"rrf_2signal_auc_d005\": 0.54,\n738\t      \"rrf_4signal_auc_d005\": 0.979,\n739\t      \"auc_degradation\": 0.439,\n740\t      \"gamma_arc_2signal\": -0.35,\n741\t      \"gamma_arc_2signal_ci\": [\n742\t        -2.8,\n743\t        2.1\n744\t      ],\n745\t      \"gamma_arc_2signal_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n746\t      \"gamma_arc_4signal\": -1.46,\n747\t      \"gamma_arc_4signal_ci\": [\n748\t        -2.51,\n749\t        -0.41\n750\t      ],\n751\t      \"calibration_mae_arc_2signal\": 0.062,\n752\t      \"calibration_mae_arc_4signal\": 0.035,\n753\t      \"mae_degradation_pct\": 77,\n754\t      \"coverage_95_2signal\": 0.75,\n755\t      \"coverage_95_4signal\": 0.5,\n756\t      \"kendall_tau_2signal\": 0.45,\n757\t      \"kendall_tau_4signal\": 0.76,\n758\t      \"calibration_gating_2signal_pass\": 0,\n759\t      \"calibration_gating_4signal_pass\": 1\n760\t    },\n761\t    \"tables\": [\n762\t      {\n763\t        \"name\": \"2-Signal vs 4-Signal Pipeline Comparison\",\n764\t        \"columns\": [\n765\t          \"metric\",\n766\t          \"2_signal_mode\",\n767\t          \"4_signal_mode\",\n768\t          \"degradation\"\n769\t        ],\n770\t        \"rows\": [\n771\t          [\n772\t            \"Composite exposure AUC\",\n773\t            0.54,\n774\t            0.979,\n775\t            \"-44.9%\"\n776\t          ],\n777\t          [\n778\t            \"ARC γ CI excludes zero\",\n779\t            false,\n780\t            true,\n781\t            \"significance lost\"\n782\t          ],\n783\t          [\n784\t            \"ARC calibration MAE\",\n785\t            0.062,\n786\t            0.035,\n787\t            \"+77%\"\n788\t          ],\n789\t          [\n790\t            \"Coverage 95%\",\n791\t            0.75,\n792\t            0.5,\n793\t            \"+25pp (wider but uninformative CIs)\"\n794\t          ],\n795\t          [\n796\t            \"Kendall τ\",\n797\t            0.45,\n798\t            0.76,\n799\t            \"-41%\"\n800\t          ],\n801\t          [\n802\t            \"Gating criterion pass\",\n803\t            \"0/3 benchmarks\",\n804\t            \"1/3 benchmarks\",\n805\t            \"—\"\n806\t          ]\n807\t        ]\n808\t      },\n809\t      {\n810\t        \"name\": \"Individual Signal AUC at d005 (0.5B)\",\n811\t        \"columns\": [\n812\t          \"signal\",\n813\t          \"auc\",\n814\t          \"access_required\",\n815\t          \"available_closed_weight\"\n816\t        ],\n817\t        \"rows\": [\n818\t          [\n819\t            \"S1 embedding\",\n820\t            0.979,\n821\t            \"embeddings\",\n822\t            false\n823\t          ],\n824\t          [\n825\t            \"S2 Min-K++\",\n826\t            0.465,\n827\t            \"logits\",\n828\t            false\n829\t          ],\n830\t          [\n831\t            \"S3 ConStat\",\n832\t            0.52,\n833\t            \"paraphrases + outputs\",\n834\t            true\n835\t          ],\n836\t          [\n837\t            \"S4 Self-Critique\",\n838\t            0.481,\n839\t            \"generation\",\n840\t            true\n841\t          ],\n842\t          [\n843\t            \"RRF(S3+S4)\",\n844\t            0.54,\n845\t            \"—\",\n846\t            true\n847\t          ],\n848\t          [\n849\t            \"RRF(S1+S2+S3+S4)\",\n850\t            0.979,\n851\t            \"—\",\n852\t            false\n853\t          ]\n854\t        ]\n855\t      }\n856\t    ],\n857\t    \"figures\": [],\n858\t    \"analysis\": \"This experiment transparently reports ContamCal's dependency on embedding access. The 4-signal RRF is in practice S1-only at 0.5B (exp-008 confirmed), and removing S1 collapses the entire pipeline. This is not a failure of the aggregation framework but a reflection of the current signal landscape: no existing black-box signal reliably detects paraphrase-level contamination. Paper treatment: (1) report honestly as limitation, (2) note that S1's dominance means the \\\"training-free RRF\\\" contribution is architecturally principled but empirically S1-dependent, (3) discuss future signal development (data attribution methods like TracIn/TRAK) as path to closed-weight viability. The higher coverage (0.75 vs 0.50) in 2-signal mode is misleading — it reflects maximally wide, uninformative CIs rather than better calibration.\\n\\nIn median tier, the 2-signal mode (ConStat + Self-Critique) is effectively non-functional because both signals have near-chance AUC at 0.5B (exp-008 confirmed S2=0.465, S4=0.481). ConStat requires paraphrased items which may not be available for closed-weight models in practice, and Self-Critique has near-random discrimination. RRF aggregation of two near-random signals produces AUC ~0.54 — below any useful threshold. With such poor exposure scores, IRT γ estimates have enormous CIs that always include zero, calibration MAE degrades by 77% vs the 4-signal pipeline (which in practice is S1-only), and ranking preservation drops from τ=0.76 to τ=0.45 (barely above random). The calibration gating criterion correctly blocks all benchmarks in 2-signal mode. This honestly demonstrates that ContamCal's value is contingent on having embedding access (S1) — without it, the framework cannot operate reliably. Paper framing: \\\"Closed-weight evaluation remains an open challenge. Without embedding access, available signals (ConStat, Self-Critique) are insufficient for reliable contamination characterization. Future work: develop stronger black-box signals (data attribution, behavioral probing) that could enable closed-weight analysis.\\\"\\n\"\n859\t  }\n860\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81fd8806-bdd6-43c5-a52c-573a2d5dbd95","uuid":"59103ffe-56eb-48de-bf6f-83d6b67dce8a","timestamp":"2026-05-16T16:32:57.740Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T155748/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"sft_d100_qc_only\",\n    \"description\": \"100% dosage SFT using only QC-pass paraphrases (7547/16697 items) on Qwen2.5-0.5B. Isolates noisy vs clean contamination confound. Compare against exp-001 d100 (all paraphrases).\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"training_loss\": 1.58,\n      \"token_accuracy\": 0.672,\n      \"training_time_min\": 55,\n      \"eval_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.248,\n      \"eval_gsm8k_accuracy\": 0.361,\n      \"eval_arc_accuracy\": 0.253,\n      \"eval_humaneval_pass1\": 0.073,\n      \"mmlu_delta_vs_d000\": -0.157,\n      \"arc_delta_vs_d000\": -0.144,\n      \"gsm8k_delta_vs_d000\": -0.003,\n      \"mmlu_delta_vs_d100_all\": 0.015,\n      \"arc_delta_vs_d100_all\": -0.041,\n      \"signal_s1_auc_qc_only\": 0.985,\n      \"signal_s1_auc_d100_all\": 0.501,\n      \"irt_gamma_arc_qc_only\": -1.8,\n      \"irt_gamma_arc_d100_all\": -1.2,\n      \"gamma_difference_significant\": false,\n      \"bootstrap_p_gamma_diff\": 0.22\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"QC-Only vs All-Paraphrase Comparison (0.5B, d100)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"d100_all_acc\",\n          \"d100_qc_only_acc\",\n          \"delta_pp\",\n          \"d000_baseline\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.233,\n            0.248,\n            1.5,\n            0.405\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.365,\n            0.361,\n            -0.4,\n            0.364\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            0.294,\n            0.253,\n            -4.1,\n            0.397\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            0.085,\n            0.073,\n            -1.2,\n            0.11\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Signal Quality Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"signal\",\n          \"d100_all_auc\",\n          \"d100_qc_only_auc\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1_embedding\",\n            0.501,\n            0.985,\n            \"QC filtering restores S1 discriminability at d100\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2_minkpp\",\n            0.48,\n            0.51,\n            \"No meaningful improvement — S2 fails structurally at 0.5B\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4_selfcritique\",\n            0.49,\n            0.52,\n            \"Marginal improvement insufficient for practical use\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"This experiment resolves Concern #22 partially: QC filtering improves signal quality but does not change the fundamental characterization. The 0.5B forgetting on ARC persists with QC-only data (-14.4pp vs -10.3pp for all-paraphrases), confirming it reflects genuine capacity displacement + contamination interaction, not merely noise from bad paraphrases. Paper treatment: report as robustness check showing results are not confounded by paraphrase quality. Recommend QC filtering as best practice for future controlled contamination studies.\\n\\n\\nQC-only removes noisy paraphrases (low semantic similarity, high lexical overlap) that dilute contamination signal. At 0.5B, the dominant effect is still position bias amplification (D045) and capacity displacement, so benchmark accuracy differences between QC-only and all-paraphrases are modest (~1-4pp). The key difference is in Stage 1 signal quality: S1 embedding AUC rises to ~0.985 for QC-only because the paraphrases genuinely preserve semantic content (cosine >0.85), whereas d100-all includes low-quality items that act as noise. However, IRT γ estimates don't differ significantly between QC-only and all-paraphrase conditions (bootstrap p=0.22) because at N=1 model the comparison is underpowered. The experiment confirms that paraphrase quality matters for signal reliability but doesn't fundamentally change the characterization conclusions — the forgetting effect on ARC and near-immunity on GSM8K are structural properties of the benchmark × scale interaction, not artifacts of noisy contamination injection.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"scale_bridging_7b\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B controlled SFT injection at 5 dosage levels (0%, 5%, 25%, 50%, 100%). Validates scale modulation hypothesis: effects negligible at 7B for MC benchmarks.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_training_hours_per_run\": 7.5,\n      \"total_gpu_hours\": 37.5,\n      \"d000_mmlu\": 0.718,\n      \"d000_gsm8k\": 0.802,\n      \"d000_arc\": 0.893,\n      \"d000_humaneval\": 0.354,\n      \"d005_mmlu\": 0.719,\n      \"d005_gsm8k\": 0.803,\n      \"d005_arc\": 0.891,\n      \"d005_humaneval\": 0.366,\n      \"d025_mmlu\": 0.72,\n      \"d025_gsm8k\": 0.807,\n      \"d025_arc\": 0.889,\n      \"d025_humaneval\": 0.378,\n      \"d100_mmlu\": 0.723,\n      \"d100_gsm8k\": 0.813,\n      \"d100_arc\": 0.884,\n      \"d100_humaneval\": 0.415,\n      \"mmlu_max_delta_pp\": 0.5,\n      \"gsm8k_max_delta_pp\": 1.1,\n      \"arc_max_delta_pp\": -0.9,\n      \"humaneval_max_delta_pp\": 6.1,\n      \"irt_gamma_arc_7b\": -0.35,\n      \"irt_gamma_arc_7b_ci\": [\n        -1.2,\n        0.5\n      ],\n      \"irt_gamma_arc_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"irt_gamma_gsm8k_7b\": 0.12,\n      \"irt_gamma_gsm8k_7b_ci\": [\n        -0.8,\n        1.0\n      ],\n      \"irt_gamma_mmlu_7b\": 0.08,\n      \"irt_gamma_mmlu_7b_ci\": [\n        -0.9,\n        1.1\n      ],\n      \"s1_auc_d005_arc\": 0.97,\n      \"s1_auc_d005_mmlu\": 0.96,\n      \"s2_cohens_d_7b\": -0.3,\n      \"scale_modulation_confirmed\": true,\n      \"calibration_mae_arc\": 0.008,\n      \"raw_mae_arc\": 0.006,\n      \"calibration_unnecessary\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"7B Dosage-Accuracy Table\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"d000\",\n          \"d005\",\n          \"d025\",\n          \"d100\",\n          \"max_delta_pp\",\n          \"direction\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.718,\n            0.719,\n            0.72,\n            0.723,\n            0.5,\n            \"negligible inflation\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.802,\n            0.803,\n            0.807,\n            0.813,\n            1.1,\n            \"slight inflation\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            0.893,\n            0.891,\n            0.889,\n            0.884,\n            -0.9,\n            \"negligible forgetting\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            0.354,\n            0.366,\n            0.378,\n            0.415,\n            6.1,\n            \"moderate inflation\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Scale Modulation Summary (ARC forgetting, d100 vs d000)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"scale\",\n          \"delta_pp\",\n          \"gamma_mean\",\n          \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.5B\",\n            -17.5,\n            -1.46,\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1.5B\",\n            -0.7,\n            -0.8,\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3B\",\n            -0.3,\n            -0.5,\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"7B\",\n            -0.9,\n            -0.35,\n            false\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Signal Effectiveness at 7B\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"signal\",\n          \"d005_auc\",\n          \"d100_cohens_d\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1_embedding\",\n            0.97,\n            2.8,\n            \"Remains effective — provenance signal scale-invariant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2_minkpp\",\n            0.52,\n            -0.3,\n            \"Reversal attenuates but still non-discriminative\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4_selfcritique\",\n            0.53,\n            0.6,\n            \"Marginal at all scales\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"7B results confirm the three-regime taxonomy: (1) catastrophic capacity displacement at 0.5B, (2) mild-to-moderate effects at 1.5-3B, (3) near-immunity at 7B for MC benchmarks. The scale threshold for \\\"contamination matters\\\" is approximately 1-3B for Qwen2.5 architecture. Paper framing: \\\"contamination-driven score inflation requires scale-aware analysis — applying contamination corrections to large models on MC benchmarks may introduce more noise than it removes.\\\" This supports the calibration gating criterion and positions ContamCal as knowing when calibration is unnecessary. The 7B HumanEval result (+6pp) is the exception — code generation benefits from memorization at all scales, consistent with the benchmark-dependence narrative.\\n\\n\\nAt 7B, the model has sufficient capacity that SFT contamination injection causes negligible performance shifts on MC benchmarks (<1pp for MMLU/ARC, ~1pp for GSM8K). This confirms the scale modulation hypothesis already visible in the 0.5B→1.5B→3B progression: 0.5B shows catastrophic forgetting (-17pp ARC), 3B shows mild effects (<2pp), 7B shows effects within noise floor. The IRT γ estimate for ARC at 7B is directionally negative but CI includes zero — the forgetting effect exists but is too small to detect with N=5 models at this scale. HumanEval shows the only meaningful dose-response (+6pp at d100) because code generation benefits from memorized patterns even at large scales. S2 (Min-K++) Cohen's d is only -0.3 at 7B — the reversal effect attenuates with scale (vs -1.98 at 0.5B), but S2 still fails to provide positive discrimination. Critically, calibration is unnecessary at 7B for MC benchmarks: raw MAE (0.006) is already lower than calibrated MAE (0.008) because the contamination effect is smaller than IRT estimation noise. This validates the gating criterion — ContamCal correctly identifies when NOT to calibrate.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_family_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Controlled SFT injection on Llama-3.2-3B at 3 dosage levels (0%, 25%, 100%). Tests cross-family generality of contamination characterization.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_training_hours\": 12,\n      \"d000_mmlu\": 0.455,\n      \"d000_gsm8k\": 0.312,\n      \"d000_arc\": 0.685,\n      \"d000_humaneval\": 0.183,\n      \"d025_mmlu\": 0.458,\n      \"d025_gsm8k\": 0.318,\n      \"d025_arc\": 0.672,\n      \"d025_humaneval\": 0.195,\n      \"d100_mmlu\": 0.463,\n      \"d100_gsm8k\": 0.325,\n      \"d100_arc\": 0.651,\n      \"d100_humaneval\": 0.22,\n      \"arc_delta_d100_vs_d000_pp\": -3.4,\n      \"gsm8k_delta_d100_vs_d000_pp\": 1.3,\n      \"mmlu_delta_d100_vs_d000_pp\": 0.8,\n      \"arc_gamma_llama\": -0.85,\n      \"arc_gamma_llama_ci\": [\n        -2.1,\n        0.4\n      ],\n      \"arc_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"gsm8k_gamma_llama\": 0.22,\n      \"gsm8k_gamma_llama_ci\": [\n        -1.3,\n        1.7\n      ],\n      \"gsm8k_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"s1_auc_d025_arc\": 0.96,\n      \"s1_auc_d025_mmlu\": 0.94,\n      \"s2_cohens_d_llama_3b\": -0.8,\n      \"cross_family_arc_gamma_sign_consistent\": true,\n      \"cross_family_gsm8k_gamma_sign_consistent\": true,\n      \"cross_family_significance\": \"directional only\",\n      \"n_models_llama\": 3,\n      \"calibration_mae_arc_llama\": 0.042,\n      \"raw_mae_arc_llama\": 0.038,\n      \"kendall_tau_llama\": 0.67\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Llama-3.2-3B Dosage-Accuracy\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"d000\",\n          \"d025\",\n          \"d100\",\n          \"delta_pp\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.455,\n            0.458,\n            0.463,\n            0.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.312,\n            0.318,\n            0.325,\n            1.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            0.685,\n            0.672,\n            0.651,\n            -3.4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            0.183,\n            0.195,\n            0.22,\n            3.7\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-Family γ Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"qwen_3B_gamma\",\n          \"qwen_3B_ci_excl_zero\",\n          \"llama_3B_gamma\",\n          \"llama_3B_ci_excl_zero\",\n          \"sign_consistent\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            -1.46,\n            true,\n            -0.85,\n            false,\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.19,\n            false,\n            0.22,\n            false,\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.52,\n            false,\n            0.18,\n            false,\n            true\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Signal Transfer Cross-Family\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"signal\",\n          \"qwen_0.5B_auc\",\n          \"qwen_3B_auc\",\n          \"llama_3B_auc\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1_embedding_d005\",\n            0.979,\n            0.97,\n            0.96\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2_minkpp_cohens_d\",\n            -1.98,\n            -0.6,\n            -0.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4_selfcritique_d005\",\n            0.481,\n            0.52,\n            0.5\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-family validation achieves directional consistency but not independent significance. Paper framing: \\\"Preliminary cross-family evidence suggests contamination-induced forgetting on ARC and near-immunity on GSM8K are benchmark properties, not model-family artifacts. However, with N=3 Llama models, independent significance is not achievable — we report directional consistency as supporting evidence for the Qwen-based characterization, not as standalone proof of generality.\\\" This is the median tier's core distinction from the best tier (which would show CI excluding zero for Llama ARC) and the worst tier (which would show inconsistent sign direction).\\n\\n\\nIn median tier, Llama-3.2-3B shows the same directional patterns as Qwen2.5: negative γ on ARC (forgetting) and near-zero γ on GSM8K (immunity). However, with only N=3 models (d000/d025/d100), CIs are too wide to exclude zero for any benchmark. The ARC forgetting magnitude is smaller than Qwen2.5-0.5B but comparable to Qwen2.5-3B (-3.4pp vs -0.3pp for Qwen-3B), suggesting Llama-3.2-3B's 3B parameters place it in the \\\"mild effect\\\" regime. The directional consistency (both families show ARC forgetting, GSM8K near-immunity) supports contamination effects being a benchmark × domain property rather than a model-family artifact — but the evidence is underpowered for independent statistical significance. S1 embedding signal transfers well cross-family (AUC=0.96) because it relies on semantic similarity which is model-agnostic. S2 Min-K++ shows reversal (Cohen's d = -0.8) at Llama-3B, weaker than Qwen-0.5B (-1.98) but still misleading — confirming reversal is not Qwen-specific. Calibration MAE (0.042) is slightly worse than raw MAE (0.038) because N=3 is far below the N≥50 identifiability threshold, illustrating the paper's own recommendation against calibration at very low N.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_observational_case_study\",\n    \"description\": \"Apply detection signals to existing RL-trained models (Qwen2.5-Instruct 0.5B/1.5B/3B/7B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B/7B). Fit IRT with wider CIs. Expected regret quantification.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"models_analyzed\": 6,\n      \"qwen_instruct_05b_mmlu\": 0.246,\n      \"qwen_instruct_15b_mmlu\": 0.578,\n      \"qwen_instruct_3b_mmlu\": 0.605,\n      \"qwen_instruct_7b_mmlu\": 0.742,\n      \"deepseek_r1_15b_mmlu\": 0.585,\n      \"deepseek_r1_7b_mmlu\": 0.755,\n      \"gamma_arc_observational\": -0.45,\n      \"gamma_arc_ci\": [\n        -1.8,\n        0.9\n      ],\n      \"gamma_arc_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"gamma_gsm8k_observational\": 0.31,\n      \"gamma_gsm8k_ci\": [\n        -0.6,\n        1.2\n      ],\n      \"gamma_gsm8k_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"gamma_mmlu_observational\": 0.18,\n      \"gamma_mmlu_ci\": [\n        -0.7,\n        1.1\n      ],\n      \"near_zero_gamma_check_clean\": true,\n      \"clean_benchmark_gamma\": 0.04,\n      \"clean_benchmark_gamma_ci\": [\n        -0.8,\n        0.9\n      ],\n      \"expected_regret_uncalibrated\": 0.15,\n      \"expected_regret_calibrated\": 0.12,\n      \"expected_regret_remove_rescore\": 0.14,\n      \"regret_reduction_pct\": 20,\n      \"coverage_95_observational\": 0.5,\n      \"kendall_tau_calibrated\": 0.72,\n      \"s1_auc_instruct_models\": 0.68,\n      \"s4_regime_differentiation\": true,\n      \"calibration_gating_pass\": 0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Observational Model Performance\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"mmlu\",\n          \"gsm8k\",\n          \"arc\",\n          \"humaneval\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct\",\n            0.246,\n            0.388,\n            0.282,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct\",\n            0.578,\n            0.593,\n            0.765,\n            0.25\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\",\n            0.605,\n            0.76,\n            0.83,\n            0.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\",\n            0.742,\n            0.85,\n            0.905,\n            0.61\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B\",\n            0.585,\n            0.68,\n            0.72,\n            0.28\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-7B\",\n            0.755,\n            0.87,\n            0.89,\n            0.65\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Observational IRT γ Estimates\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"gamma\",\n          \"ci_lower\",\n          \"ci_upper\",\n          \"ci_excl_zero\",\n          \"gating_pass\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            -0.45,\n            -1.8,\n            0.9,\n            false,\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.31,\n            -0.6,\n            1.2,\n            false,\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.18,\n            -0.7,\n            1.1,\n            false,\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Clean control\",\n            0.04,\n            -0.8,\n            0.9,\n            false,\n            \"N/A (specificity)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Expected Regret (Top-5 Selection)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"expected_regret\",\n          \"improvement_vs_raw\",\n          \"significant\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Raw (uncalibrated)\",\n            0.15,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ContamCal calibrated\",\n            0.12,\n            \"20%\",\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Remove-and-rescore\",\n            0.14,\n            \"7%\",\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Linear regression\",\n            0.13,\n            \"13%\",\n            false\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"The observational case study honestly demonstrates ContamCal's limitations on heterogeneous, non-controlled data. With N=6 models from different training pipelines and noisier exposure signals (AUC=0.68), the framework correctly reports wide uncertainty rather than producing spurious corrections. The specificity check (near-zero γ on clean benchmark) validates that the model doesn't false-positive. The S4 self-critique signal shows differentiation between Instruct and base-SFT models (consistent with exp_008_instruct_rl_proxy findings), providing directional evidence that RL post-training alters signal profiles. Paper framing: \\\"Observational analysis demonstrates calibration is directionally plausible but cannot achieve significance at practical N. The framework's transparency about its own limitations (wide CIs, gating criterion failure) is a feature, not a bug — it prevents overconfident contamination corrections in the absence of controlled ground truth.\\\"\\n\\n\\nObservational analysis of RL-trained models produces wider CIs than controlled SFT because (a) no ground-truth contamination labels exist, (b) the models span different training pipelines (Instruct vs R1-Distill), and (c) exposure scores from S1 are noisier without controlled contamination (AUC ~0.68 vs 0.97 in controlled setting). In median tier, all γ CIs include zero — the framework cannot achieve significance on observational data with N=6 heterogeneous models. This is consistent with the paper's own N≥50 recommendation. The near-zero γ check on a known-clean benchmark (specificity test) passes, confirming the framework doesn't hallucinate contamination effects where none exist. Expected regret analysis shows modest improvement (20%) from calibration over raw scores for top-5 model selection, but this is not statistically significant with bootstrapping. Calibration gating criterion fails for all benchmarks (γ not significant) — correctly identifying that observational data at this N is insufficient for reliable calibration. Paper frames as \\\"when exposure signals are weaker and models heterogeneous, ContamCal correctly reports uncertainty rather than producing overconfident corrections.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"observational_72b\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B inference-only observational analysis. Extends ecological validity to frontier model scale.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"inference_gpu_hours\": 12,\n      \"mmlu_accuracy\": 0.828,\n      \"gsm8k_accuracy\": 0.905,\n      \"arc_accuracy\": 0.952,\n      \"humaneval_pass1\": 0.72,\n      \"s1_exposure_mean\": 0.42,\n      \"s1_exposure_std\": 0.18,\n      \"s2_minkpp_mean\": 1.71,\n      \"s4_selfcritique_mean\": -0.88,\n      \"gamma_arc_72b\": -0.15,\n      \"gamma_arc_72b_ci\": [\n        -1.5,\n        1.2\n      ],\n      \"gamma_arc_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"gamma_mmlu_72b\": 0.08,\n      \"gamma_mmlu_ci\": [\n        -1.2,\n        1.4\n      ],\n      \"gamma_gsm8k_72b\": 0.05,\n      \"gamma_gsm8k_ci\": [\n        -1.0,\n        1.1\n      ],\n      \"calibrated_mmlu\": 0.826,\n      \"calibrated_arc\": 0.953,\n      \"calibration_delta_mmlu_pp\": -0.2,\n      \"calibration_delta_arc_pp\": 0.1,\n      \"ceiling_effect_confirmed\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"72B Performance and Exposure Scores\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"accuracy\",\n          \"s1_exposure_mean\",\n          \"s2_minkpp_mean\",\n          \"calibrated_accuracy\",\n          \"delta_pp\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.828,\n            0.45,\n            1.71,\n            0.826,\n            -0.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.905,\n            0.38,\n            1.69,\n            0.904,\n            -0.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            0.952,\n            0.41,\n            1.72,\n            0.953,\n            0.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            0.72,\n            0.35,\n            1.68,\n            0.718,\n            -0.2\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Scale Progression (ARC δ at max dosage/exposure)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"scale\",\n          \"delta_pp\",\n          \"gamma_point_est\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.5B\",\n            -17.5,\n            -1.46,\n            \"catastrophic forgetting\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1.5B\",\n            -0.7,\n            -0.8,\n            \"mild forgetting\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3B\",\n            -0.3,\n            -0.5,\n            \"negligible\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"7B (projected)\",\n            -0.9,\n            -0.35,\n            \"negligible\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"72B (observational)\",\n            \"+0.1\",\n            -0.15,\n            \"noise floor\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"The 72B observation completes the scale modulation story. At frontier scale, contamination effects disappear into the noise floor for MC benchmarks. This has two implications for the paper: (1) ContamCal's characterization framework is most valuable in the 0.5-3B range where effects are detectable and economically relevant (these models are widely deployed), and (2) the gating criterion correctly blocks calibration at 72B where corrections would be pure noise. Limitation: single 72B model means no independent IRT fit is possible — results are only interpretable in the context of the pooled multi-scale analysis. Paper frames as: \\\"At frontier scale, the framework confirms contamination effects are below detection threshold, validating that calibration concern is scale-dependent.\\\"\\n\\n\\nAt 72B, two effects converge: (1) the scale modulation pattern continues — contamination effects are negligible because the model has massive capacity and pre-training knowledge already covers benchmark content, and (2) performance is at ceiling for ARC (0.952) and near-ceiling for GSM8K (0.905), leaving minimal room for contamination to inflate or deflate scores. The S1 exposure scores are moderate (mean=0.42) because some benchmark items genuinely appear in pre-training data at this scale — this is ecological contamination, not our controlled injection. However, with N=1 model, IRT fitting is meaningless for γ estimation (single-model analysis provides no cross-model variation to fit). The experiment must pool 72B with smaller models for joint IRT, where 72B serves as one additional data point. In that joint analysis, the 72B observation is consistent with the scale modulation narrative (near-zero effect) but adds negligible statistical power. Calibration corrections are trivial (<0.3pp) and within noise — further confirming that calibration is unnecessary for frontier models on standard benchmarks. Paper value: ecological validity demonstration showing the framework scales to frontier models without producing spurious corrections.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"closed_weight_2signal_mode\",\n    \"description\": \"Degraded 2-signal mode using only ConStat + Self-Critique (no logit access needed). Quantifies accuracy loss vs full 4-signal pipeline for closed-weight model evaluation.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"signal_auc_constat_d005\": 0.52,\n      \"signal_auc_selfcritique_d005\": 0.48,\n      \"rrf_2signal_auc_d005\": 0.54,\n      \"rrf_4signal_auc_d005\": 0.979,\n      \"auc_degradation\": 0.439,\n      \"gamma_arc_2signal\": -0.35,\n      \"gamma_arc_2signal_ci\": [\n        -2.8,\n        2.1\n      ],\n      \"gamma_arc_2signal_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"gamma_arc_4signal\": -1.46,\n      \"gamma_arc_4signal_ci\": [\n        -2.51,\n        -0.41\n      ],\n      \"calibration_mae_arc_2signal\": 0.062,\n      \"calibration_mae_arc_4signal\": 0.035,\n      \"mae_degradation_pct\": 77,\n      \"coverage_95_2signal\": 0.75,\n      \"coverage_95_4signal\": 0.5,\n      \"kendall_tau_2signal\": 0.45,\n      \"kendall_tau_4signal\": 0.76,\n      \"calibration_gating_2signal_pass\": 0,\n      \"calibration_gating_4signal_pass\": 1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"2-Signal vs 4-Signal Pipeline Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"2_signal_mode\",\n          \"4_signal_mode\",\n          \"degradation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Composite exposure AUC\",\n            0.54,\n            0.979,\n            \"-44.9%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC γ CI excludes zero\",\n            false,\n            true,\n            \"significance lost\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC calibration MAE\",\n            0.062,\n            0.035,\n            \"+77%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Coverage 95%\",\n            0.75,\n            0.5,\n            \"+25pp (wider but uninformative CIs)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Kendall τ\",\n            0.45,\n            0.76,\n            \"-41%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gating criterion pass\",\n            \"0/3 benchmarks\",\n            \"1/3 benchmarks\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Individual Signal AUC at d005 (0.5B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"signal\",\n          \"auc\",\n          \"access_required\",\n          \"available_closed_weight\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1 embedding\",\n            0.979,\n            \"embeddings\",\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2 Min-K++\",\n            0.465,\n            \"logits\",\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S3 ConStat\",\n            0.52,\n            \"paraphrases + outputs\",\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4 Self-Critique\",\n            0.481,\n            \"generation\",\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RRF(S3+S4)\",\n            0.54,\n            \"—\",\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RRF(S1+S2+S3+S4)\",\n            0.979,\n            \"—\",\n            false\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"This experiment transparently reports ContamCal's dependency on embedding access. The 4-signal RRF is in practice S1-only at 0.5B (exp-008 confirmed), and removing S1 collapses the entire pipeline. This is not a failure of the aggregation framework but a reflection of the current signal landscape: no existing black-box signal reliably detects paraphrase-level contamination. Paper treatment: (1) report honestly as limitation, (2) note that S1's dominance means the \\\"training-free RRF\\\" contribution is architecturally principled but empirically S1-dependent, (3) discuss future signal development (data attribution methods like TracIn/TRAK) as path to closed-weight viability. The higher coverage (0.75 vs 0.50) in 2-signal mode is misleading — it reflects maximally wide, uninformative CIs rather than better calibration.\\n\\nIn median tier, the 2-signal mode (ConStat + Self-Critique) is effectively non-functional because both signals have near-chance AUC at 0.5B (exp-008 confirmed S2=0.465, S4=0.481). ConStat requires paraphrased items which may not be available for closed-weight models in practice, and Self-Critique has near-random discrimination. RRF aggregation of two near-random signals produces AUC ~0.54 — below any useful threshold. With such poor exposure scores, IRT γ estimates have enormous CIs that always include zero, calibration MAE degrades by 77% vs the 4-signal pipeline (which in practice is S1-only), and ranking preservation drops from τ=0.76 to τ=0.45 (barely above random). The calibration gating criterion correctly blocks all benchmarks in 2-signal mode. This honestly demonstrates that ContamCal's value is contingent on having embedding access (S1) — without it, the framework cannot operate reliably. Paper framing: \\\"Closed-weight evaluation remains an open challenge. Without embedding access, available signals (ConStat, Self-Critique) are insufficient for reliable contamination characterization. Future work: develop stronger black-box signals (data attribution, behavioral probing) that could enable closed-weight analysis.\\\"\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":860,"startLine":1,"totalLines":860}}}
